type: software
title: "ai-layered-control: A Systems-Engineering Reference Architecture for Layered Closed-Loop AI Control"
abstract: "A fast-slow reference architecture for layered closed-loop AI control, built on strict fast/slow authority decoupling: the slow-loop AI gets no actuator authority, and the deterministic fast loop alone writes the actuator command. A 10 Hz qualitative supervisor is commissioned from 36 labeled macro-windows, stores 15 scalars (60 B) as prototypes, exposes a distance-based confidence and abstains explicitly outside its manifold. The frozen supervisor is paired with a 12 B three-knob physical tuning tuple for constrained on-site calibration, and with a 1 kHz 32 B blanking residual probe that rejects broadband innovation while freezing through stimulation and commutation artifacts. A 96 B zero-dynamic-memory ANSI C99 gatekeeper owns the 1 kHz command through four anti-windup control banks, seven observable gate states, cumulative severe-fault latching and a 7-bit audit mask. Python and MATLAB/Simulink C-MEX paths replay the same frozen core, with domain interface mappings for Industrial WAAM, Edge VLA, and Closed-Loop Neuromodulation."
